<!-- ======================== HEADER ======================== -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="header-inner">
    <div class="report-tag">Policy Research Report</div>
    <h1>Global Cost of Living Crisis Index 2026</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A Comparative Analysis of Economic Stress, Affordability Gaps, and Structural Drivers Across 80 Major Cities Worldwide</p>
    <div class="header-meta">
      <span>📅 Data Year: 2026</span>
      <span>🌍 80 Cities Analyzed</span>
      <span>📊 Baseline: New York, USA (Index = 100)</span>
      <span>👥 Audience: Policy Analysts &amp; Economic Researchers</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- TOC -->
  <div class="toc">
    <h3>Table of Contents</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#exec-overview">Executive Overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="#regional">Regional Cost-of-Living Comparison</a></li>
      <li><a href="#affordability">Affordability and Rent Burden Analysis</a></li>
      <li><a href="#crisis-tiers">Crisis Tier Profiling</a></li>
      <li><a href="#inflation-oil">Inflation and Oil Shock Exposure</a></li>
      <li><a href="#findings">Key Findings and Policy Implications</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================== SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW ======================== -->
  <div class="section" id="exec-overview">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">Section 01</div>
      <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
      <p>A headline snapshot of the global cost-of-living landscape in 2026, presenting the five key performance indicators and the distribution of economic stress across crisis tiers.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- KPI Cards -->
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Median Cost of Living Index</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">65.5</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">vs. New York = 100 baseline</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card warn">
        <div class="kpi-label">Avg Rent-to-Salary Ratio</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">61.5%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Mean across all 80 cities</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card danger">
        <div class="kpi-label">Purchasing Power Gap</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">148.7</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Basel (183.7) − Beirut (35.0)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card danger">
        <div class="kpi-label">High-Crisis City Count</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">14</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Cities in Tier 5 (most severe)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card warn">
        <div class="kpi-label">Avg Annual Inflation Rate</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">8.3%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Mean across all 80 cities (2025)</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Context -->
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Crisis Tier Distribution (80 Cities)</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrap short">
          <canvas id="tierDistChart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Cost of Living Index — Global Distribution</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrap short">
          <canvas id="colDistChart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Highlight boxes -->
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="highlight-box">
        <h4>Most Expensive City</h4>
        <p>Zurich, Switzerland leads globally with a cost of living index of <strong>118.5</strong>, supported by an average monthly net salary of $7,200 — yet rent still consumes <strong>70.8%</strong> of income.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="highlight-box red">
        <h4>Deepest Crisis</h4>
        <p>Buenos Aires, Argentina is experiencing <strong>150% annual inflation</strong>. Cairo (28%), Karachi/Lahore (28.5%), and Lagos (34%) face structural hyperinflationary conditions with salaries as low as $165/month.</p>
      </div>
